{"title":"2020 USAMO Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/7/317096889b84df0b72bf69ceb4c82208305f1b0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\ge 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"46\" height=\"16\" /> be an integer. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/6/a56e07178e131066071b642c6ab64bc86a19a3ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1 \\ge x_2 \\ge \\cdots \\ge x_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"151\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/d/75ddf0321d8e308e69a517b93f9cd34e7b34446a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_1 \\ge y_2 \\ge \\cdots \\ge y_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"143\" height=\"15\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/3/f93f5c51ea4b04b4992b003b39479f29018f6bda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2n$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" /> real numbers such that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/4/c74a4291b90375ef7ee7f4f92c2391fb35ebacba.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} 0 &amp;= x_1 + x_2 + \\cdots + x_n = y_1 + y_2 + \\cdots + y_n\\\\ \\text{and  }1 &amp;= x_1^2+x_2^2+\\cdots+x_n^2=y_1^2+y_2^2+\\cdots+y_n^2. \\end{align*}\" width=\"376\" height=\"44\" />\nProve that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/e/b8ef79881bc4fa74d5bb69f1970d760d716598aa.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{i=1}^n(x_iy_i-x_iy_{n+1-i})\\ge\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{n-1}}.\\]\" width=\"247\" height=\"47\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/0/17076704107b48b586b6a3eedbf9ba90d9baa3f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u_i = x_i - x_{n+1-i}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"131\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/e/84ed8b1a1cb57afa653b6fc9bfa10c0f68f1061b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v_i = y_i - y_{n+1-i}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"127\" height=\"16\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/d/3fd77e67d5e894bf1026f4cffd551f2856f52af0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\le i \\le n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"74\" height=\"15\" />. \n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/6/a56e07178e131066071b642c6ab64bc86a19a3ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1 \\ge x_2 \\ge \\cdots \\ge x_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"151\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/d/75ddf0321d8e308e69a517b93f9cd34e7b34446a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_1 \\ge y_2 \\ge \\cdots \\ge y_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"143\" height=\"15\" />, both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/1/3e1c2b6fc6e36508ff46015c800d93ba0b9b9861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(u_i)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"32\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/4/ac4ccdfd531b2fd81cba5a13c9df845cae053502.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(v_i)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"30\" height=\"20\" /> are non-increasing sequences satisfying <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/b/c8b4826c8e8bdf5ece269d82e9d24d8064f7c552.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u_{n+1-i} = -u_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"107\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/6/b86ecd4fa5afa42e8d4ec0ccad4e5cb494e35948.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v_{n+1-i} = -v_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"104\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>We can express the target sum in terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/f/5afd2dd74b7100b3d32eaff06aec8cb1178eeea6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/f/85ffd98b4eaea58a8db38fd0047e3a1d7c5661a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/7/b17063fad20b7bfad8d4882f905e0de096d00e4e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{i=1}^n (x_i y_i - x_i y_{n+1-i}) = \\sum_{i=1}^n x_i v_i = \\frac{1}{2} \\sum_{i=1}^n u_i v_i\\]\" width=\"339\" height=\"47\" />\n</p><p>By the Rearrangement Inequality, because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/b/68bf834c92ff6b73fe05a57f8f6ee1db9459f5c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(y_i)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"18\" /> is non-increasing and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/d/90dd4353ab5f8fc3761bb3db09dfefb362d0a451.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(y_{n+1-i})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"66\" height=\"20\" /> is non-decreasing:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/6/466128cc6cc057bd08c00a35c5b886d2a19418de.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{i=1}^n y_i y_{n+1-i} \\le \\frac{1}{n}\\left(\\sum_{i=1}^n y_i\\right)^2 = 0\\]\" width=\"246\" height=\"57\" />\n</p><p>This gives a lower bound on the sum of squares of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/f/85ffd98b4eaea58a8db38fd0047e3a1d7c5661a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$v_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/d/15d7bedcd840c6d9f3e753dcdadf25d2053f262a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{i=1}^n v_i^2 = 2\\sum_{i=1}^n y_i^2 - 2\\sum_{i=1}^n y_i y_{n+1-i} \\ge 2\\]\" width=\"287\" height=\"47\" />\n</p><p>Similarly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/c/ccce7cc6e064866c1c124c7c65ffecdfb468265a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{i=1}^n u_i^2 \\ge 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"82\" height=\"53\" />.\n</p><p>Applying summation by parts along with the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality for ordered sequences subject to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/d/61dd86a619e88ec98105c367a524fa0430bd8f26.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum x_i = \\sum y_i = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"147\" height=\"31\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/9/97980e7601f2672b05fbd296862326c512b16fd6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum x_i^2 = \\sum y_i^2 = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"152\" height=\"31\" /> yields:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/e/91e881f150e3e7d5d0751b2bc358aa2b50ea67ab.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{2} \\sum_{i=1}^n u_i v_i \\ge \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{n-1}}\\]\" width=\"157\" height=\"47\" />\n</p><p>Equality is achieved when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/0/e903393eb9eaa58b4011176fd3ef1b151e3796fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1 = y_1 = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"113\" height=\"43\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/8/138c6c00d1f2b61c938a213317b3ea6da905083e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_n = y_n = -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"130\" height=\"43\" />, and all remaining middle variables are equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_USAMO\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2020 USAMO\">2020 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"2020 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=2020\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2020 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\"><b>Last Problem</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2020 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2020 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2020 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2020 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2020 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018013301\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.031 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.050 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 192/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1261/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 54/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5883/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.750      1 -total\n 55.95%    7.133      1 Template:USAMO_newbox\n 41.50%    5.291      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:22584:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018013301 and revision id 291180. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}